[.lesson-title]
THE KINGBIRD.

. The kingbird is not bigger than
a robin.
. He eats flies, and worms, and
bugs, and berries.
. He builds his nest in a tree, near
some house.
. When there are young ones in
the nest, he sits on the top of a tree
near them.
. He watches to see that no bird
comes to hurt them or their mother.
// page 42
. If a hawk, a crow, or even an
eagle comes near, he makes a dash
at it.
. Though he is so small, he is
brave, and he is also very active.
. He never fails to drive off other
birds from his nest.
. He flies around and around the
eagle, and suddenly strikes him with
his sharp bill.
. He strikes at his eye, and then
darts away before the eagle can catch
him.
. Or he strikes from behind, and
is off again before the eagle can turn
round.
. In a short time, the great eagle
is tired of such hard blows, and flies
away. He is very glad to get rid of
his foe.
. Is not the little fellow a brave
bird?
. Because he can drive off all other
birds, he is called the [.sc]#kingbird#.

